[% META
   title = "Manual inventory: assemblies, parts, and BOM"
   description = "Step-by-step: create two master units (base and add-on), every printed part and hardware item, and attach them on the BOM so an order can explode to prints and purchases."
   roles = "admin,developer"
   TemplateType = "Documentation"
   category = "inventory,3d-printing,bom"
   page_version = "0.1"
   last_updated = "Sat Aug 22 2026"
   site_specific = "false"
   project_id = "42"
   project_code = "Inventory"
%]
[% PageVersion = 'Documentation/InventoryInternalBuildBom.tt,v 0.1 2026/08/22 hermes-agent Exp - manual assembly BOM entry' %]
[% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %][% PageVersion %][% END %]

<div class="container">
    [% INCLUDE 'admin/documentation/_doc_header.tt'
        page_title   = 'Manual inventory: assemblies, parts, and BOM'
        site_name    = site_name
        user_role    = user_role
        last_updated = last_updated
        page_name    = page_name
        doc_project_id   = project_id
        doc_project_code = project_code %]

    <div id="toc" class="row doc-toc">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 class="doc-h2">Quick Navigation</h2>
            <p class="doc-muted">Jump to section:</p>
            <div class="doc-navrow">
                <a href="#overview" class="doc-navlink">Overview</a>
                <a href="#prep" class="doc-navlink">Prepare</a>
                <a href="#masters" class="doc-navlink">Master units</a>
                <a href="#parts" class="doc-navlink">Printed parts</a>
                <a href="#hardware" class="doc-navlink">Hardware</a>
                <a href="#bom" class="doc-navlink">Attach BOM</a>
                <a href="#options" class="doc-navlink">Options</a>
                <a href="#check" class="doc-navlink">Check</a>
                <a href="#hdry" class="doc-navlink">HDRY example</a>
                <a href="#see-also" class="doc-navlink">See Also</a>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="overview" class="doc-h2">1. Overview</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">This is the <strong>manual Inventory path</strong> for an internal
            3D build (not for sale, or later for sale). You type every item in the UI.
            Do not treat one downloaded 3MF as one product. The assembly PDF is the BOM.</p>
            <p class="doc-body">Two <strong>master</strong> items (assemblable):</p>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Base unit</strong> — structure + bottom + top + wheels.</li>
                <li><strong>Add-on module</strong> — structure only (no bottom or top).</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-body">Each master’s BOM lists printed parts (qty often &gt; 1)
            and purchased hardware. When a unit is ordered, that BOM is what you
            buy and what you queue to print.</p>
            <div class="doc-info">
                <p class="doc-body">Routes below are from
                <code>Controller::Inventory</code>:
                <code>/Inventory/item/add</code>,
                <code>/Inventory/item/view/&lt;id&gt;</code>,
                <code>/Inventory/item/edit/&lt;id&gt;</code>,
                <code>/Inventory/bom/&lt;parent_id&gt;</code>,
                <code>/Inventory/bom/add/&lt;parent_id&gt;</code> (POST),
                <code>/Inventory/bom/list</code>.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="prep" class="doc-h2">2. Prepare (before any Add Item)</h2>
            <ol class="doc-body">
                <li>Open the assembly PDF. List every printed label (FLS01, BLS01, …)
                    and every hardware line (screws, bearings, magnets, gasket, Polydryer).
                    Note qty <em>per base</em> vs <em>per add-on</em>.</li>
                <li>Decide sitename (3d site owns 3d builds). Stay logged in on that Host.</li>
                <li>Have File Manager rows for the 3MF/STL/PDF if you will link models later
                    (<a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/DryerProjectPlan') %]" class="doc-link">Dryer project plan</a>).</li>
                <li>Confirm filament spools already exist (e.g. PETG White). Create those
                    first if missing:
                    <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Inventory/item/add') %]" class="doc-link">/Inventory/item/add</a>,
                    category <code>3d_filament</code> or Filament, origin purchased, unit <code>g</code>.</li>
            </ol>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="masters" class="doc-h2">3. Create the two master items</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Do this twice — once for Base, once for Add-on.</p>
            <ol class="doc-body">
                <li>Go to
                    <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Inventory/item/add') %]" class="doc-link">/Inventory/item/add</a>.</li>
                <li>SKU examples: <code>INT-HDRY-BASE</code> and <code>INT-HDRY-MOD</code>.</li>
                <li>Name: e.g. “HDRY Base unit (bottom, top, wheels)” and
                    “HDRY Add-on module (no bottom/top)”.</li>
                <li>Category: <code>3dStock</code> or similar. Origin: <code>3d_printed</code>
                    (the assembly is made in-house even though some lines are purchased).</li>
                <li>Unit: <code>each</code>.</li>
                <li>Tick <strong>Has BOM / Recipe?</strong> (<code>is_assemblable</code>).
                    Without this, BOM add will refuse the item.</li>
                <li>Leave shop flags off. The add form does not expose
                    <code>show_in_shop</code>; default is hidden. Do not list in marketplace.</li>
                <li>Save. You land on the item list or the item view. Write down the new
                    <code>id</code> from
                    <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Inventory/item/view') %]" class="doc-link">/Inventory/item/view/&lt;id&gt;</a>.</li>
                <li>Open
                    <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Inventory/bom') %]" class="doc-link">/Inventory/bom/&lt;id&gt;</a>
                    for that master. It will be empty until you add components.</li>
            </ol>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="parts" class="doc-h2">4. Create each printed part (one item per PDF label)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">One inventory item per distinct printed piece. If the PDF
            needs four of FLS01, that is <strong>qty 4 on the BOM</strong>, not four items.</p>
            <ol class="doc-body">
                <li><a href="[% c.uri_for('/Inventory/item/add') %]" class="doc-link">Add item</a>.</li>
                <li>SKU: include the label, e.g. <code>INT-HDRY-FLS01</code>.</li>
                <li>Name: the label plus a short English name from the manual.</li>
                <li>Category: <code>3d_printed_item</code> or <code>3dStock</code>.</li>
                <li>Origin: <code>3d_printed</code>. Unit: <code>each</code>.</li>
                <li>Tick <strong>Print on Demand</strong> if the form shows it
                    (<code>requires_printing</code>). If save ignores that field
                    (add handler may not persist 3D-only columns), note it on the item
                    and set filament type PETG in notes until Inventory edit grows those fields.</li>
                <li>Do <strong>not</strong> tick Has BOM on a single printed part unless
                    that part itself is an assembly.</li>
                <li>Save. Record id + SKU + which master(s) need it + qty.</li>
                <li>Later (3D side): upload/extract the STL for that label on
                    the model library and set <code>item_id</code> to this part.
                    That is
                    <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/3dPrintingPlan') %]" class="doc-link">3dPrintingPlan</a>
                    work, not this page.</li>
            </ol>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="hardware" class="doc-h2">5. Create hardware (purchased) items</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Same add form. Origin <code>purchased</code>.
            Category <code>Hardware</code> or <code>3d_supply</code>. Not assemblable.
            Not print-on-demand.</p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr><th class="doc-th">Example SKU</th><th class="doc-th">Name</th><th class="doc-th">Unit</th><th class="doc-th">Notes (HDRY per module)</th></tr>
                <tr><td class="doc-td">HW-M4-14</td><td class="doc-td">Screw M4 14 mm</td><td class="doc-td">each</td><td class="doc-td">180</td></tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt"><td class="doc-td">HW-M3-20</td><td class="doc-td">Screw M3 20 mm</td><td class="doc-td">each</td><td class="doc-td">16</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="doc-td">HW-608ZZ</td><td class="doc-td">Bearing 608zz</td><td class="doc-td">each</td><td class="doc-td">16</td></tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt"><td class="doc-td">HW-MAG-8X2</td><td class="doc-td">Magnet 8×2 mm</td><td class="doc-td">each</td><td class="doc-td">20</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="doc-td">HW-GASKET-6X3</td><td class="doc-td">Adhesive gasket 6×3 mm</td><td class="doc-td">m</td><td class="doc-td">6 m</td></tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt"><td class="doc-td">HW-POLYDRYER</td><td class="doc-td">Polydryer</td><td class="doc-td">each</td><td class="doc-td">1</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="doc-td">HW-WHEEL-KIT</td><td class="doc-td">Wheel washer/bolt/nut/spacer</td><td class="doc-td">each</td><td class="doc-td">base unit only</td></tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-body">Receive stock later at
            <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Inventory/stock/receive') %]" class="doc-link">/Inventory/stock/receive</a>
            when the box of screws arrives.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="bom" class="doc-h2">6. Attach every component to a master</h2>
            <ol class="doc-body">
                <li>Open
                    <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Inventory/bom/list') %]" class="doc-link">/Inventory/bom/list</a>
                    and click the Base master (must show as assemblable).</li>
                <li>On
                    <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Inventory/bom') %]" class="doc-link">/Inventory/bom/&lt;base_id&gt;</a>
                    use the add-component form. That POSTs to
                    <code>/Inventory/bom/add/&lt;base_id&gt;</code>.</li>
                <li>For each printed part and hardware line: pick the component item,
                    set <strong>quantity</strong> from the PDF, unit <code>each</code>
                    (or <code>m</code> / <code>g</code> as appropriate).</li>
                <li>Tick <strong>optional</strong> only for true options
                    (AMS support, rollers, dryer gadget, doors, drawer). Those can
                    live on the master as optional BOM lines, or on a third
                    “option kit” master — pick one convention and keep it.</li>
                <li>Repeat the whole BOM attach on the Add-on master.
                    Omit bottom, top, wheels, and wheel hardware.</li>
                <li>If add fails with “not marked as assemblable”, edit the master
                    and tick Has BOM, then retry.</li>
            </ol>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="options" class="doc-h2">7. Option kits (optional third master)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">If AMS/Hydra, rollers, or dryer extras should be
            ordered on their own, create another assemblable item
            (e.g. <code>INT-HDRY-AMS</code>) and BOM only those parts.
            An order for “base + AMS” then explodes two masters.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="check" class="doc-h2">8. Check before you queue prints</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li>Both masters appear on
                    <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Inventory/bom/list') %]" class="doc-link">/Inventory/bom/list</a>.</li>
                <li>Base BOM has structure + bottom + top + wheels + hardware.</li>
                <li>Add-on BOM has structure + hardware, no bottom/top/wheels.</li>
                <li>Printed part qty matches the PDF (not “1 per 3MF file”).</li>
                <li>Each printed part will get an STL and a
                    <code>printing_3d_models</code> row later; do not queue a job
                    named “Module 1.3mf”.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="hdry" class="doc-h2">9. HDRY numbers from the manual (starting list)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Source: assembly manual 1 Feb 2025. Complete the
            printed-label table from the PDF; 29 codes are already visible
            (FLS01/02, BLS01/02, BBL01/02, …). Hardware per module is in
            <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/DryerProjectPlan') %]" class="doc-link">DryerProjectPlan</a>
            §1b.</p>
            <p class="doc-body">Do not reuse inventory item 51
            <code>INT-HDRY-001</code> as a master if it still means “one row per 3MF”.
            Either retarget that SKU or create BASE/MOD and leave 51 as a file-catalog
            leftover.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <div id="see-also" class="doc-success">
                <h2 class="doc-h3">See Also</h2>
                <ul class="doc-body">
                    <li><a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/Inventory') %]" class="doc-link">Inventory (module overview)</a></li>
                    <li><a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/3dPrintingPlan') %]" class="doc-link">3D printing coordinator plan</a></li>
                    <li><a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/DryerProjectPlan') %]" class="doc-link">Dryer project plan</a></li>
                    <li><a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/3d_printing') %]" class="doc-link">3d_printing operator KB</a></li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <div class="doc-footer">
                <p>Inventory how-to (project #42). 3D planning links here; it does not replace 3dPrintingPlan.</p>
                <p><em>This documentation is part of the Comserv system.</em></p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
